01:10:09.100 --> 01:10:14.100
So would like to, more about from you.

01:10:14.320 --> 01:10:19.320
- I mean, I think the, I
haven't read Wilkerson's book.

01:10:19.400 --> 01:10:24.290
The to me, the what's distinctive about

01:10:25.710 --> 01:10:29.140
slavery in the Americas after 1600

01:10:29.140 --> 01:10:33.211
is the demographic change
that the indigenous people

01:10:33.211 --> 01:10:35.777
have been wiped out to such a large extent

01:10:35.777 --> 01:10:40.030
and that the population is
replaced with the African slaves.

01:10:40.030 --> 01:10:43.840
All of the examples I'm talking about are

01:10:43.840 --> 01:10:48.840
slaves are a source of labor.

01:10:48.860 --> 01:10:52.150
And also in many cases, more importantly,

01:10:52.150 --> 01:10:54.140
a source of children.

01:10:54.140 --> 01:10:58.060
There's "The Cambridge World
