01:11:03.220 --> 01:11:07.170
and in many societies around the world

01:11:07.170 --> 01:11:10.500
there are more women slaves
than there are male slaves.

01:11:10.500 --> 01:11:14.280
So that you know that and
scholars of slavery work on this.

01:11:14.280 --> 01:11:17.690
My colleague Ed Rugemer
is one of the people that

01:11:17.690 --> 01:11:19.930
they're aware of, there's a lot of variety

01:11:19.930 --> 01:11:24.770
for in how slaves are
used in different places.

01:11:24.770 --> 01:11:28.240
In the year 1000, any society that

01:11:28.240 --> 01:11:30.010
doesn't have enough goods to export

01:11:30.010 --> 01:11:31.900
starts exporting either its people

01:11:31.900 --> 01:11:34.660
or people it's captured
from its neighbors.

01:11:34.660 --> 01:11:37.720
So it's just the world is short of labor

01:11:37.720 --> 01:11:39.420
and everybody will pay money for it.

01:11:39.420 --> 01:11:42.600
So it's a very appealing commodity,

01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:45.433
a grim, grim as this is to us today.

